Water and sanitation sources — complete books, methods and operating evidence (@wu-sources: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation) { r_7AMRJFFR11FF35KJM7Y7M05B3M
Begin with the Portuguese [Manual de Saneamento — Funasa, fifth edition](sources/Manual-de-Saneamento-Funasa.lingua#r_65G5YY3QVCA8HAXMPC8RTPKEWE) and the complete [Introduction to Drinking Water Treatment — TU Delft](sources/Introduction-to-Drinking-Water-Treatment-TU-Delft.lingua#r_0XXF9PBVKKD6FWSJRVDTCKQXP4) course. Work the physical design argument in [The Physics of Water Treatment Design — AguaClara](sources/Physics-of-Water-Treatment-Design-AguaClara.lingua#r_1V2KMP22J5KMQF65K8Q7ZXXBAR) as treatment becomes quantitative. The [Guidelines for drinking-water quality — WHO, 2026 consolidated edition](sources/Drinking-Water-Quality-WHO-2026.lingua#r_71BB45J2CZ76C0WZ6H1C7SWZ5F) guidance and [Potabilidade e vigilância da água — Ministério da Saúde](sources/Potabilidade-e-Vigilancia-Vigiagua.lingua#r_0MJJ4WY69D303TQ11X6TNZZ779) references supply public-health and jurisdictional context; their purposes differ from a calculation of hydraulic capacity or removal efficiency.

The biological-treatment volumes, [Biological Wastewater Treatment — Chen and colleagues, second edition](sources/Biological-Wastewater-Treatment-Chen-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_1AE9DK0YWQR5GDECZ9KK1JJP37) and [Assessment of Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data — von Sperling, Verbyla and Oliveira](sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS) support sustained wastewater and evidence study. [Water and Wastewater Treatment Engineering — MIT 1.85](sources/Water-and-Wastewater-Treatment-Engineering-MIT.lingua#r_396YEC55H29CR6J4ZBZX5JBY60) supplies graduate problems and design work. [Industrial Water Treatment Operation and Maintenance — UFC 3-230-13](sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R) connects industrial water chemistry with continuing operation; [WaterTAP — inspectable water-treatment models](sources/WaterTAP-Process-Models.lingua#r_6JCG0EJT4DZTWJTNKZQXF1Y3JD) makes more detailed process models inspectable.

Read each source's edition and access notes. Authorized free reading, permission to redistribute and permission to adapt are distinct. A public course may assign copyrighted books that it does not provide. Keep each selected version and its notices when retaining it in a personal library. All books, PDFs, software, datasets, recordings and standards are external references.

